# Written into the source tree by the policy harnesses for whichever policy is
# being checked, and never part of a contribution. A run killed by a signal
# leaves them behind, where `git add -A` will sweep them into a commit -- which
# has happened once, and shipped a stale ladder that no longer elaborates.
